  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Sir Martin Stuart Sorrell (born 14 February 1945) is a British businessman and the founder of WPP plc.  Sorrell was the longest-serving chief executive of a FTSE 100 company.\nHe was consistently one of the UK's highest-paid corporate executives. According to The Sunday Times Rich List in 2019, Sorrell was worth £368 million. Sorrell has served on boards and advisory bodies of a number of high-profile public, academic and business organisations, including several leading business schools, both in the UK and internationally.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
